            "mimeType": "application/json; charset=UTF-8",
            "text": "{\"hits\":[{\"id\":1768609,\"kind\":\"scheduled\",\"category\":\"film_media\",\"subcategory\":\"film\",\"type\":\"screening\",\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"state\":\"published\",\"venue_type\":null,\"organization_id\":58,\"billetto_score\":null,\"name\":\"History on Film: La Haine (1995)\",\"name_truncated\":\"History on Film: La Haine (1995)\",\"description\":\"FREE ENTRY, booking is essential. Join us for a 30 th anniversary screening of La Haine , a powerful tale of young people processing and navigating the aftermath of an uprising in Paris’ outskirts, les banlieues , their home and their very futures. Visually stunning, La Haine was both critically acclaimed upon its release in 1995 film, winning a French film academy award for Best Film, and Kassowitz a win as Best Director at Cannes, and a cult classic, considered a masterful exploration of class, social tension and racism in contemporary France. Whether for a first viewing, or another rewatch, this is a rare opportunity to see La Haine (1995) on the big screen, and consider its messages and impact thirty years on. As usual, we'll follow the screening with a post-film discussion. Come for the film, stay for the conversation. All welcome! Don’t miss out on a night where history and art intersect.\",\"price\":0.0,\"price_range\":\"Free\",\"image\":\"https://billetto.imgix.net/twimdzz9fc2kwtfclce5bup0qmqt?w=640&h=360&fit=crop&auto=compress%2Cformat&rect=0%2C39%2C2060%2C1159&s=0e5a8ea54fbf8ef2dfee81ceab82f1a3\",\"uses_generic_billetto_image\":false,\"keywords\":[],\"organizer_id\":5342150,\"organizer_image\":\"https://billetto.imgix.net/o6br5uqs1om4sk6ud4ifh2xp90xe?s=434767ee2914c4f6d079b78a45d4b360\",\"url\":\"https://billetto.co.uk/e/history-on-film-la-haine-1995-tickets-1768609\",\"brand\":\"Black @ Gold : Goldsmiths Black History\",\"stock\":4535,\"on_sale\":true,\"total_clicks\":99136,\"starts_at\":\"Dec 12 2026 18:30\",\"ends_at\":\"Dec 12 2026 22:30\",\"hide_end_date\":false,\"country\":\"United Kingdom\",\"macroregion\":\"London\",\"region\":\"Inner London — East\",\"subregion\":\"Lewisham and Southwark\",\"neighborhood\":null,\"city\":\"London\",\"postal_code\":146,\"location\":\"Richard Hoggart Building, Goldsmiths, London\",\"location_slug\":\"london\",\"venue_name\":\"Richard Hoggart Building, Goldsmiths\",\"published_time\":1765197941,\"created_at\":1765197941,\"start_time\":1765564200,\"end_time\":1797114600,\"unique\":false,\"quick_buy\":false,\"major_purchase\":false,\"experience_more_enabled\":false,\"experience_more_code\":null,\"experience_more_limit\":null,\"promoted\":true,\"billetto_advertising_percentage\":33.0,\"bucket\":\"No Advertising\",\"average_advertised_ticket_price\":0.0,\"time_zone\":\"Europe/London\",\"year\":2026,\"week_number\":50,\"weekend_event\":true,\"org_channel_discovery\":true,\"org_channel_email\":true,\"ba_tickets_sold\":0,\"ba_tickets_remaining\":1138,\"ba_tickets_limit_reached\":false,\"short_header\":\"History on Film: La Haine (199\",\"short_description\":\"FREE ENTRY, booking is essential. Join us for a 30 th anniversary scre\",\"video_url\":null,\"square_banner\":null,\"portrait_banner\":null,\"alternative_banner\":null,\"age_rating\":null,\"billetto_weighting\":133.0,\"local_dates\":[20261212],\"event_availability\":\"high\",\"schema\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"http://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Event\\\",\\\"eventAttendanceMode\\\":\\\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\\\",\\\"endDate\\\":\\\"2026-12-12T23:30:00+01:00\\\",\\\"eventStatus\\\":\\\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\\\",\\\"isAccessibleForFree\\\":true,\\\"organizer\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Black @ Gold : Goldsmiths Black History\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://billetto.co.uk/users/black-gold-goldsmiths-black-history\\\"},\\\"location\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Place\\\",\\\"address\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"PostalAddress\\\",\\\"addressCountry\\\":\\\"United Kingdom\\\",\\\"addressLocality\\\":\\\"London\\\",\\\"addressRegion\\\":\\\"Inner London — East\\\",\\\"postalCode\\\":\\\"SE14 6NW\\\",\\\"streetAddress\\\":\\\"Lewisham Way\\\"},\\\"name\\\":\\\"Richard Hoggart Building, Goldsmiths\\\",\\\"geo\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"GeoCoordinates\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":51.475,\\\"longitude\\\":-0.0351}},\\\"identifier\\\":\\\"1768609\\\",\\\"offers\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Offer\\\",\\\"availability\\\":\\\"http://schema.org/InStock\\\",\\\"price\\\":\\\"0.0\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"History on Film: La Haine (1995)\\\",\\\"priceCurrency\\\":\\\"GBP\\\",\\\"validFrom\\\":\\\"2025-12-08T13:18:55+01:00\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://billetto.co.uk/e/history-on-film-la-haine-1995-tickets-1768609\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"FREE ENTRY, booking is essential. Join us for a 30 th anniversary screening of La Haine , a powerful tale of young people processing and navigating the aftermath of an uprising in Paris’ outskirts, les banlieues , their home and t...\\\",\\\"startDate\\\":\\\"2025-12-12T19:30:00+01:00\\\",\\\"image\\\":[\\\"https://billetto.imgix.net/twimdzz9fc2kwtfclce5bup0qmqt?w=640\\\\u0026h=360\\\\u0026fit=crop\\\\u0026auto=compress%2Cformat\\\\u0026rect=0%2C39%2C2060%2C1159\\\\u0026ar=1%3A1\\\\u0026crop=faces\\\\u0026s=1fdd68f0ace4327e770eed1bb824d5e7\\\",\\\"https://billetto.imgix.net/twimdzz9fc2kwtfclce5bup0qmqt?w=640\\\\u0026h=360\\\\u0026fit=crop\\\\u0026auto=compress%2Cformat\\\\u0026rect=0%2C39%2C2060%2C1159\\\\u0026ar=4%3A3\\\\u0026crop=faces\\\\u0026s=c7e8fc57855c8b02a2cf9a8f2adc9033\\\",\\\"https://billetto.imgix.net/twimdzz9fc2kwtfclce5bup0qmqt?w=640\\\\u0026h=360\\\\u0026fit=crop\\\\u0026auto=compress%2Cformat\\\\u0026rect=0%2C39%2C2060%2C1159\\\\u0026ar=16%3A9\\\\u0026crop=faces\\\\u0026s=4d41107d83361bb7ab3e41c9b3dfce95\\\"],\\\"name\\\":\\\"History on Film: La Haine (1995)\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://billetto.co.uk/e/history-on-film-la-haine-1995-tickets-1768609\\\"}\",\"total_organizer_revenue\":\"0.0\",\"premium\":false,\"eqs_score\":39.14,\"host_ids\":[5342150],\"_tags\":[],\"culture_pass_enabled\":false,\"_geoloc\":{\"lng\":-0.0351,\"lat\":51.475},\"objectID\":\"1768609\",\"_highlightResult\":{\"category\":{\"value\":\"film_media\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"subcategory\":{\"value\":\"film\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"type\":{\"value\":\"screening\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"name\":{\"value\":\"History on Film: La Haine (1995)\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"description\":{\"value\":\"FREE ENTRY, booking is essential. Join us for a 30 th anniversary screening of La Haine , a powerful tale of young people processing and navigating the aftermath of an uprising in Paris’ outskirts, les banlieues , their home and their very futures. Visually stunning, La Haine was both critically acclaimed upon its release in 1995 film, winning a French film academy award for Best Film, and Kassowitz a win as Best Director at Cannes, and a cult classic, considered a masterful exploration of class, social tension and racism in contemporary France. Whether for a first viewing, or another rewatch, this is a rare opportunity to see La Haine (1995) on the big screen, and consider its messages and impact thirty years on. As usual, we'll follow the screening with a post-film discussion. Come for the film, stay for the conversation. All welcome! Don’t miss out on a night where history and art intersect.\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"brand\":{\"value\":\"Black @ Gold : Goldsmiths Black History\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"city\":{\"value\":\"London\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"location_slug\":{\"value\":\"london\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"venue_name\":{\"value\":\"Richard Hoggart Building, Goldsmiths\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]}}},{\"id\":2048027,\"kind\":\"regular\",\"category\":\"charity\",\"subcategory\":\"international_aid\",\"type\":\"screening\",\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"state\":\"published\",\"venue_type\":null,\"organization_id\":58,\"billetto_score\":null,\"name\":\"The Killing of Awdah Hathaleen | Film screening and conversation with Aziz Hathaleen\",\"name_truncated\":\"The Killing of Awdah Hathaleen | Film…\",\"description\":\"Join the Britain Palestine Project for a public screening of Palestinian human rights organisation Al-Haq’s investigative film The Killing of Awdah Hathaleen: Beyond a Settler Crime , followed by a conversation with Awdah’s brother, Aziz Hathaleen and Zainah Haroun from Al-Haq. Awdah was a Palestinian teacher, father of three and human rights defender who contributed to the Oscar-winning documentary No Other Land . On 28 July 2025, he was shot and killed while filming a settler attack in his village of Umm al-Kheir, in Masafer Yatta in the occupied West Bank. Using video footage and a reconstruction of the scene, Al-Haq’s film examines the circumstances of Awdah’s killing and places it in the wider context of settler violence in the West Bank. After the screening, we’ll hear from Aziz about his brother and what life is like for the community of Umm al-Kheir today. Tickets are free and everyone is welcome. Please reserve your place through Billetto. Guests will be invited to make an optional donation on the night to support the community of Umm al-Kheir.\",\"price\":0.0,\"price_range\":\"Free\",\"image\":\"https://billetto.imgix.net/19buhzpa39j6xs71uw8zmrfdvio8?w=640&h=360&fit=crop&auto=compress%2Cformat&rect=0%2C50%2C960%2C540&s=90a0cfd3c971d789c7a542881fbaf026\",\"uses_generic_billetto_image\":false,\"keywords\":[],\"organizer_id\":4427429,\"organizer_image\":\"https://billetto.imgix.net/b0q9lcgh3cx4ulsizctshfxfl8rh?s=2272ad4ae78a4c31a6584444c77c171b\",\"url\":\"https://billetto.co.uk/e/the-killing-of-awdah-hathaleen-film-screening-and-conversation-with-aziz-hathaleen-tickets-2048027\",\"brand\":\"Britain Palestine Project\",\"stock\":200,\"on_sale\":true,\"total_clicks\":4,\"starts_at\":\"Nov 17 2026 18:00\",\"ends_at\":\"Nov 17 2026 20:00\",\"hide_end_date\":true,\"country\":\"United Kingdom\",\"macroregion\":\"London\",\"region\":\"Inner London — East\",\"subregion\":\"Lambeth\",\"neighborhood\":null,\"city\":\"London\",\"postal_code\":18,\"location\":\"St John’s Church, Waterloo, London\",\"location_slug\":\"london\",\"venue_name\":\"St John’s Church, Waterloo\",\"published_time\":1794224177,\"created_at\":1794224177,\"start_time\":1794938400,\"end_time\":1794945600,\"unique\":false,\"quick_buy\":false,\"major_purchase\":false,\"experience_more_enabled\":false,\"experience_more_code\":null,\"experience_more_limit\":null,\"promoted\":true,\"billetto_advertising_percentage\":33.0,\"bucket\":\"Free event\",\"average_advertised_ticket_price\":0.0,\"time_zone\":\"Europe/London\",\"year\":2026,\"week_number\":47,\"weekend_event\":false,\"org_channel_discovery\":true,\"org_channel_email\":true,\"ba_tickets_sold\":0,\"ba_tickets_remaining\":66,\"ba_tickets_limit_reached\":false,\"short_header\":\"The Killing of Awdah Hathaleen\",\"short_description\":\"Join the Britain Palestine Project for a public screening of Palestini\",\"video_url\":null,\"square_banner\":null,\"portrait_banner\":null,\"alternative_banner\":null,\"age_rating\":null,\"billetto_weighting\":133.0,\"local_dates\":[20261117],\"event_availability\":\"high\",\"schema\":\"{\\\"@context\\\":\\\"http://schema.org\\\",\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Event\\\",\\\"eventAttendanceMode\\\":\\\"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode\\\",\\\"endDate\\\":\\\"2026-11-17T20:00:00+00:00\\\",\\\"eventStatus\\\":\\\"https://schema.org/EventScheduled\\\",\\\"isAccessibleForFree\\\":true,\\\"organizer\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Organization\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Britain Palestine Project\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://billetto.co.uk/users/britain-palestine-project\\\"},\\\"location\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Place\\\",\\\"address\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"PostalAddress\\\",\\\"addressCountry\\\":\\\"United Kingdom\\\",\\\"addressLocality\\\":\\\"London\\\",\\\"addressRegion\\\":\\\"Inner London — East\\\",\\\"postalCode\\\":\\\"SE1 8TY\\\",\\\"streetAddress\\\":\\\"London SE1 8TY\\\"},\\\"name\\\":\\\"St John’s Church, Waterloo\\\",\\\"geo\\\":{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"GeoCoordinates\\\",\\\"latitude\\\":51.5045,\\\"longitude\\\":-0.112}},\\\"identifier\\\":\\\"2048027\\\",\\\"offers\\\":[{\\\"@type\\\":\\\"Offer\\\",\\\"availability\\\":\\\"http://schema.org/InStock\\\",\\\"price\\\":\\\"0.0\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"General\\\",\\\"priceCurrency\\\":\\\"GBP\\\",\\\"validFrom\\\":\\\"2026-11-09T11:23:53+00:00\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://billetto.co.uk/e/the-killing-of-awdah-hathaleen-film-screening-and-conversation-with-aziz-hathaleen-tickets-2048027\\\"}],\\\"description\\\":\\\"Join the Britain Palestine Project for a public screening of Palestinian human rights organisation Al-Haq’s investigative film The Killing of Awdah Hathaleen: Beyond a Settler Crime , followed by a conversation with Awdah’s brothe...\\\",\\\"startDate\\\":\\\"2026-11-17T18:00:00+00:00\\\",\\\"image\\\":[\\\"https://billetto.imgix.net/19buhzpa39j6xs71uw8zmrfdvio8?w=640\\\\u0026h=360\\\\u0026fit=crop\\\\u0026auto=compress%2Cformat\\\\u0026rect=0%2C50%2C960%2C540\\\\u0026ar=1%3A1\\\\u0026crop=faces\\\\u0026s=745589282bbe226a1cb18375f185fdeb\\\",\\\"https://billetto.imgix.net/19buhzpa39j6xs71uw8zmrfdvio8?w=640\\\\u0026h=360\\\\u0026fit=crop\\\\u0026auto=compress%2Cformat\\\\u0026rect=0%2C50%2C960%2C540\\\\u0026ar=4%3A3\\\\u0026crop=faces\\\\u0026s=107aa8d91e5d8d5767230a296b38757e\\\",\\\"https://billetto.imgix.net/19buhzpa39j6xs71uw8zmrfdvio8?w=640\\\\u0026h=360\\\\u0026fit=crop\\\\u0026auto=compress%2Cformat\\\\u0026rect=0%2C50%2C960%2C540\\\\u0026ar=16%3A9\\\\u0026crop=faces\\\\u0026s=56c9a90449a173e076bd6a46895e4d33\\\"],\\\"name\\\":\\\"The Killing of Awdah Hathaleen | Film screening and conversation with Aziz Hathaleen\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://billetto.co.uk/e/the-killing-of-awdah-hathaleen-film-screening-and-conversation-with-aziz-hathaleen-tickets-2048027\\\"}\",\"total_organizer_revenue\":\"21112.0\",\"premium\":false,\"eqs_score\":33.43,\"host_ids\":[4427429],\"_tags\":[],\"culture_pass_enabled\":false,\"_geoloc\":{\"lng\":-0.112,\"lat\":51.5045},\"objectID\":\"2048027\",\"_highlightResult\":{\"category\":{\"value\":\"charity\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"subcategory\":{\"value\":\"international_aid\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"type\":{\"value\":\"screening\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"name\":{\"value\":\"The Killing of Awdah Hathaleen | Film screening and conversation with Aziz Hathaleen\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"description\":{\"value\":\"Join the Britain Palestine Project for a public screening of Palestinian human rights organisation Al-Haq’s investigative film The Killing of Awdah Hathaleen: Beyond a Settler Crime , followed by a conversation with Awdah’s brother, Aziz Hathaleen and Zainah Haroun from Al-Haq. Awdah was a Palestinian teacher, father of three and human rights defender who contributed to the Oscar-winning documentary No Other Land . On 28 July 2025, he was shot and killed while filming a settler attack in his village of Umm al-Kheir, in Masafer Yatta in the occupied West Bank. Using video footage and a reconstruction of the scene, Al-Haq’s film examines the circumstances of Awdah’s killing and places it in the wider context of settler violence in the West Bank. After the screening, we’ll hear from Aziz about his brother and what life is like for the community of Umm al-Kheir today. Tickets are free and everyone is welcome. Please reserve your place through Billetto. Guests will be invited to make an optional donation on the night to support the community of Umm al-Kheir.\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"brand\":{\"value\":\"Britain Palestine Project\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"city\":{\"value\":\"London\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"location_slug\":{\"value\":\"london\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]},\"venue_name\":{\"value\":\"St John’s Church, Waterloo\",\"matchLevel\":\"none\",\"matchedWords\":[]}}},{\"id\":2023696,\"kind\":\"regular\",\"category\":\"religion\",\"subcategory\":\"mysticism_occult\",\"type\":\"screening\",\"currency\":\"GBP\",\"state\":\"published\",\"venue_type\":null,\"organization_id\":58,\"billetto_score\":null,\"name\":\"Magic in the Mundane Documentary Screening with QnA\",\"name_truncated\":\"Magic in the Mundane Documentary…\",\"description\":\"Super excited to bring ' Magic in the Mundane' to the Electric Palace Cinema in Hastings! There will be a full QnA after the screening from director Leigh Brooks & guests. We will also be sharing an exclusive sneak peak at the sequel ' Sacred in the Profane' which is currently being shot around the UK, Europe and Egypt. \\\"Magic in the Mundane\\\" is a cinematic journey into the overlooked miracles of everyday existence. Filmed across breathtaking landscapes and intimate spaces, this feature length documentary gathers philosophers, writers, psychedelic guides, death doulas, trauma workers, ritual keepers, pilgrims, pantheists, pagans, monotheists and thinkers to explore where wonder lives when we're not looking for it. The film ventures into the nature of consciousness itself, asking whether artificial minds might one day perceive the sacred and how psychedelics can dissolve the veil between the self and what lies beyond it. It sits with death not as an ending but as a threshold, examines how trauma fractures and forges spiritual sight, and follows ancient and modern pilgrims alike as they walk toward meaning. Through ceremony and ritual, it seeks what broken spiritual memory has forgotten, while pantheism and paganism offer frameworks where divinity breathes through every stone and stream. Through stunning on-location cinematography and an evocative original score, these voices converge without consensus. Nothing is definitive. Each topic remains an open door, an invitation to wonder. The documentary refuses easy answers, trusting the audience to step through ... or not. Who are we when no one is watching? The magic was never elsewhere. It was always here, waiting for us to notice. Magic in the Mundane contains discussions surrounding trauma, addiction, mental health, psychedelics, grief, spirituality, and emotional healing. Some viewers may find certain testimonies and ceremonial sequences emotionally intense. The film presents a range of personal beliefs and lived experiences without advocating any particular worldview or practice.\",\"price\":12.0,\"price_range\":\"12 GBP\",\"image\":\"https://billetto.imgix.net/jjl5zdc1ra68a8m28s0d7b73b0v5?w=640&h=360&fit=crop&auto=compress%2Cformat&rect=0%2C0%2C2098%2C1180&s=4e0d374c32f1076256a8e8049a9beb49\",\"uses_generic_billetto_image\":false,\"keywords\":[],\"organizer_id\":7259999,\"organizer_image\":\"https://billetto.imgix.net/gw6tptjuj2k6p2u69o6cgigwh2y0?s=f913ad0163a7e4356a3ea009e863315a\",\"url\":\"https://billetto.co.uk/e/magic-in-the-mundane-documentary-screening-with-qna-tickets-2023696\",\"brand\":\"Leigh Brooks\",\"stock\":48,\"on_sale\":true,\"total_clicks\":252,\"starts_at\":\"Nov 18 2026 19:00\",\"ends_at\":\"Nov 18 2026 22:00\",\"hide_end_date\":false,\"country\":\"United Kingdom\",\"macroregion\":\"South East (England)\",\"region\":\"Surrey, East and West Sussex\",\"subregion\":\"East Sussex CC\",\"neighborhood\":null,\"city\":\"Hastings\",\"postal_code\":343,\"location\":\"Electric Palace Cinema, Hastings\",\"location_slug\":null,\"venue_name\":\"Electric Palace Cinema\",\"published_time\":1791030464,\"created_at\":1791030464,\"start_time\":1795028400,\"end_time\":1795039200,\"unique\":false,\"quick_buy\":false,\"major_purchase\":false,\"experience_more_enabled\":false,\"experience_more_code\":null,\"experience_more_limit\":null,\"promoted\":true,\"billetto_advertising_percentage\":33.0,\"bucket\":\"Low\",\"average_advertise